## 4. Quick sanity-check against common styles

| Style | Shield layers (real) | What the function returns |
|-------|----------------------|----------------------------|
| **OSM-Bright** | `highway-shield-us-interstate`, `highway-shield-us-highway`, `highway-shield-us-state`, `highway-shield-road` | ✅ all detected (core signature present; `icon-text-fit` absent but not required) |
| **OSM-Liberty** | `highway-shield-us-interstate`, `highway-shield-us-highway`, `highway-shield-us-state`, `highway-shield-road` | ✅ same as above |
| **OpenMapTiles** | `transportation_name` (shield sub-layers) | ✅ detected – `icon-image` uses `{network}_{ref_length}` and `text-field` uses `{ref}` |
| **A custom POI style** (e.g., `city-label`, `park-label`) | None | ❌ not detected – `icon-image` is a static name (`city`, `park`) and `text-field` is `{name}` |
| **A custom point-symbol that uses a placeholder for a different purpose** (e.g., `icon-image: "category_{type}"`, `text-field: "{type}"`) | Not a shield | ✅ still flagged as a shield because the core signature matches. If you *know* you have such layers, add an extra guard (e.g., require that the placeholder be `ref` **or** that the source-layer name contains `transportation`/`road`). |

