Below is a concise checklist, a ready-to-paste JavaScript function that implements it, and an explanation of why each cue matters.

---

## 1. Why the current heuristic fails

| Property | Typical value for many point-symbol layers | Typical value for shield layers |
|----------|--------------------------------------------|---------------------------------|
| `text-anchor` | **undefined** → defaults to `"center"` (most POI / place-name layers never set it) | Often **explicitly set** to `"center"` (or left undefined) – the same as above |
| `symbol-placement` | `"point"` for any point-symbol (places, POIs, icons) | `"point"` **or** a zoom-function (`{stops: …}`) that switches to `"line"` at higher zooms – the simple equality test will miss the latter |

Result: **high false-positive rate** (plain place-name layers) and **high false-negative rate** (real shields that use a function or set `text-anchor` explicitly).

